  "scope": "Core inspect_group_recovery_batch owns one bounded reservation index and the complete original row order: native owner/plan admission, numeric maximum observation, successor reservation insertion, execution-order proof, then complete per-group inspection. The actual SQLite adapter uses both batch and member pipelines. Fourteen two-group database states from eight flow forms exercise 364 frozen comparisons with either group corrupted and conflicting native faults; all metadata, effect, dispatch, group and branch tables remain unchanged. Native consumers cover count/slot limits, duplicates, zero and overflow, move-only local owners/errors, every reached callback and iterator unwind, and late proof/commit failure blocking checkpoint handoff. Summaries expose counts and maxima only after complete success, not identities, receipts or execution grants. The original bounded SQL snapshot, owner/plan admission, authentic authority, cold-slot original-watermark proofs and final atomic commit remain adapter responsibilities. No wire/schema change, saved-code evaluation, fuel, dispatch, watermark repair, complete native durable VM or repository extraction is introduced.",
